# Security Rules (7 Rules)

## 1. Cloudflare Protection
Put Cloudflare in front of every site: DNS, CDN, DDoS, Bot Fight Mode, WAF rules, rate limit on forms. SSL mode must be Full (strict).

## 2. Cloudflare + Vercel Acknowledgment
Vercel recommends against proxy setups. Confirm the team accepts this configuration.

## 3. Security Headers
Set in vercel.json: HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, X-Frame-Options.

## 4. Secrets Management
Secrets ONLY in Vercel env vars and 1Password. NEVER in Git or frontend code.

## 5. Sanity CORS
Limit CORS to production domains only. Read token ONLY on server side.

## 6. GitHub Security
2FA required, protect main branch, secret scanning on, Dependabot enabled, npm audit in CI.

## 7. No Leftovers
Remove test endpoints, staging links, unused packages before launch.
